{"id": 25, "ts": 1781191383.365077, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I respect Sarah\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fC\u2019s decision\u2011making and reliability, but the lack of any concrete evidence of his responsibility or role\u2011maturity in high\u2011risk international flights is a serious gap for a long\u2011distance pilot. Moreover, his difficulty communicating ideas and the egocentric reputation raise concerns about crew cooperation in the cockpit.\nCandidate\u202fB, on the other hand, is explicitly noted as \u201cvery conscientious\u201d (a strong indicator of operational reliability) and \u201chandles stress very well,\u201d which addresses our stress\u2011resilience criterion. His ability to assess weather conditions and his excellent computer skills are directly relevant to the technical and cognitive demands of long\u2011haul operations. While Sarah flagged B\u2019s \u201cpretentious\u201d demeanor and occasional wrong tone, these communication issues are less severe than C\u2019s documented difficulty articulating ideas and the risk that an egocentric attitude could undermine crew coordination.\nGiven the missing responsibility evidence for C and the comparatively stronger, documented reliability and stress\u2011handling profile of B, I would shift my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fB** as the safer overall fit."}
