{"id": 106, "ts": 1781192218.2505322, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the strongest overall fit.\u202fWe have clear evidence that C makes correct decisions quickly, stays calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology, and creates a positive atmosphere with the crew\u2014exactly the decision\u2011quality, stress\u2011resilience, technical competence, and crew\u2011cooperation we need for long\u2011distance ops.\u202fBy contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while very conscientious and good at stress handling and weather assessment, still lacks any documented example of decision\u2011quality in safety\u2011critical situations, which is a non\u2011negotiable gap.\u202fMoreover, B\u2019s weak numeric memory and documented nasty remarks raise concerns about attention to detail and professional communication, both essential for international flights.\u202fAlthough we still lack direct evidence of C\u2019s responsibility or role\u2011maturity for high\u2011risk international flights, the combination of proven decision\u2011quality and crew\u2011cooperation outweighs the missing piece, especially given that B\u2019s decision\u2011quality is unproven.\u202fTherefore, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fC, while noting that we should seek any additional confirmation of C\u2019s responsibility before finalizing."}
