{"id": 110, "ts": 1781192318.4996889, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s quick, correct decisions and crew\u2011atmosphere strengths, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the better overall fit for our long\u2011distance role.\u202fB\u2019s record shows he is **very conscientious** and **handles stress very well**, both essential for the reliability and stress\u2011resilience we need on international routes.\u202fHis ability to **assess weather conditions** and his **excellent computer skills** give him solid technical competence for complex, long\u2011haul operations.\u202fWhile B\u2019s communication style can be pretentious and occasionally adopts the wrong tone, these are behavioral issues we can address through coaching, and they do not outweigh the proven reliability and stress handling he demonstrates.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC, although calm and technically capable, is described as **egocentric**, **has difficulty communicating ideas**, and is **not very willing to further his education**\u2014a concerning limitation for a role that demands continuous learning and strong crew collaboration.\u202fMoreover, we still lack any concrete evidence of C\u2019s responsibility or maturity for high\u2011risk international flights.\u202fGiven B\u2019s demonstrated conscientiousness, stress resilience, and technical aptitude, I keep my vote for **Candidate\u202fB**."}
