{"id": 114, "ts": 1781192372.669068, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s focus on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s conscientiousness and stress resilience, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit for our long\u2011distance role.\u202fC\u2019s record shows he makes correct decisions quickly, is 100\u202f% reliable, and consistently creates a positive atmosphere with his crew\u2014key indicators of both decision quality and crew cooperation.\u202fWhile B\u2019s technical skills and stress handling are solid, his documented grumpy, uncooperative behavior and pretentious tone pose a higher risk to the collaborative cockpit environment we need on international flights.\u202fIn contrast, C\u2019s communication challenges and egocentric style, though concerning, are less likely to undermine safety than outright uncooperativeness, and can be addressed through targeted coaching.\u202fGiven the paramount importance of reliable decision\u2011making and crew harmony, I keep my vote for **Candidate\u202fC**."}
